# PX4 params for the raptor twin (sim). One file per vehicle: everything this vehicle always flies with. Mode overlays
# (ekf2_vision, ekf2_flow_range) are listed AFTER it in the scenario (`px4.params: [raptor, ekf2_vision]`, later wins).
# Format: NAME VALUE MAV_PARAM_TYPE (6 INT32, 9 REAL32). Names/ranges checked against the pinned PX4 tag (PX4_TAG, ADR-003).

# --- Collision prevention (Position mode), same as iris.params ---------------------------------------------------------
CP_DIST        1.5  9   # m. Minimum distance PX4 keeps to an obstacle in Position mode; <= 0 turns collision prevention off
CP_DELAY       0.4  9   # s. Sensor + actuation delay PX4 allows for when braking
CP_GUIDE_ANG   30.0 9   # deg. Tolerance for slipping past an obstacle instead of stopping dead
CP_GO_NO_DATA  0    6   # 0 = allow flight where the map has no data; 1 = forbid it

# --- Rate loop: SIM ONLY. Never load these rows onto the real Pixracer (QGC) -------------------------------------------
# They fit the sim's placeholder plant (Pegasus' Iris thrust curve on the raptor's 0.8 kg / 7x smaller inertia / ~half
# arms), not the real 5" whoop; the real tune is Phase 4 (docs/todo.md). The gazebo-classic_iris gains limit-cycled on this
# body at takeoff (tests/hover_stability.py 2026-10-11: rate std roll 31 / pitch 106 / yaw 96 deg/s). Per unit of PX4 output
# the raptor gets ~2.5x the Iris' roll, ~3x pitch, ~6x yaw angular acceleration, so the Iris values (in the comment) are
# divided by about that: rate std 0.3 deg/s, attitude std < 0.1 deg (PASS).
MC_ROLLRATE_P   0.06    9   # 0.15
MC_ROLLRATE_I   0.08    9   # 0.2
MC_ROLLRATE_D   0.0012  9   # 0.003
MC_PITCHRATE_P  0.05    9   # 0.15
MC_PITCHRATE_I  0.067   9   # 0.2
MC_PITCHRATE_D  0.001   9   # 0.003
MC_YAWRATE_P    0.04    9   # 0.2
MC_YAWRATE_I    0.02    9   # 0.1
